@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-1 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/ceaa000d8f9e.smy@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "It now opens with the thing a Rust developer recognises: a dependency pinned to an exact version, a lock held across an await, a test that builds its own fixture." }
~ Open with the thing a Rust developer recognises: a dependency pinned to an exact version, a lock held across …

To make the documentation relatable and understandable for Rust developers.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-2 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/ceaa000d8f9e.smy@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Then what the tool does, shown rather than described, with real output from this repository:" }
~ Show what the tool does rather than describe it.

To provide clear and practical information about the tool's functionality.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-3 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/ceaa000d8f9e.smy@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": decline, "ingest:quote": "Answering \"why is this like this?\" was dropped as a product claim." }
~ Drop the claim of answering 'why is this like this?' as a product feature.

To focus on the tool's actual capabilities rather than unmet claims.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-4 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/ceaa000d8f9e.smy@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The tool assigns labels, sources and statuses; the model proposes wording only." }
~ Assign labels, sources and statuses; the model proposes wording only.

To maintain control over the integrity of recorded information.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-5 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/ceaa000d8f9e.smy@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Staleness is attached to code identity rather than to line ranges, so a function that moved is not stale and one that changed is." }
~ Detect staleness by item body hash rather than line ranges.

To accurately track changes in code identity rather than just line positions.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-6 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/ceaa000d8f9e.smy@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Review as records. Confirming writes an attestation, rejecting writes a withdrawal whose reason unit says why, closing writes a resolution. The log keeps everything." }
~ Record review as confirmations, withdrawals with reasons, and closures with notes.

To keep a comprehensive log of all reviews and decisions made.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-7 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/ceaa000d8f9e.smy@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "It ships its own instrument. `bench` measures the model *you* chose on *your* commits, and every published figure names the model it came from — including four experiments that failed and are listed so nobody repeats them." }
~ Ship its own instrument for benchmarking the model.

To provide users with the ability to measure the performance of their chosen models on their own commits.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-8 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/ceaa000d8f9e.smy@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Two thirds of the commands never call a model. Those are the ones worth your time today: they are deterministic, tested, and cost nothing to run." }
~ Focus on deterministic commands over model-dependent ones.

To prioritize commands that are reliable, tested, and cost-effective to run.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-9 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/ceaa000d8f9e.smy@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The figures are published, naming the model each came from, including the experiments that failed." }
~ Publish figures naming the model each came from, including failed experiments.

To provide transparency about which models were tested and their results, including any failures.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-10 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/ceaa000d8f9e.smy@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Over-production is the failure mode that matters. A corpus of 54 decisions for a four-decision commit is worse than no corpus, and prompt wording was measured twice as not being the lever." }
~ Highlight over-production as the failure mode that matters.

To emphasize the importance of avoiding unnecessary or excessive output in the tool's operations.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-11 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/ceaa000d8f9e.smy@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": The hook only queues and `--estimate` prices a run before it starts. }
~ Meaningfully price extraction runs before starting them.

To inform users about the cost of extraction runs before they start, allowing them to make informed decisions.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-12 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/ceaa000d8f9e.smy@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": A cloned corpus is someone else's claim. Units carry the status the tool gave them; read `speculative` as what it says. }
~ Label cloned corpora as someone else's claims.

To clarify the status of units in cloned corpora, indicating that they are not the tool's own claims.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-13 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/dec7c232f8ba.smy@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": Research the truncated-change problem before building for it }
~ Research the truncated-change problem before building for it

The commit message states that research was done to understand the truncated-change problem, which is a significant issue affecting 59% of held-out changes.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-14 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/dec7c232f8ba.smy@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": Reporting what was left out costs nothing and is honest }
~ Reporting what was left out costs nothing and is honest

The commit message suggests that reporting what was left out is a cost-free and honest approach to dealing with the truncated-change problem.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-15 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/dec7c232f8ba.smy@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Choosing which 400 lines to show, by how much corpus attaches to each file, costs no extra call and can be measured deterministically on the held-out set" }
~ Choosing which 400 lines to show, by how much corpus attaches to each file, costs no extra call and can …

The commit message proposes a method for choosing which 400 lines to show, which is cost-effective and can be measured deterministically.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-16 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/dec7c232f8ba.smy@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Splitting the change across calls triples the cost and should wait until the two cheap ones are measured, because they may make it unnecessary" }
~ Splitting the change across calls triples the cost and should wait until the two cheap ones are measured

The commit message suggests that splitting the change across multiple calls is expensive and should be avoided unless cheaper methods prove ineffective.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-17 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/dec7c232f8ba.smy@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": The tool's promise is that it operates as designed }
~ The tool's promise is that it operates as designed

The commit message states that the tool promises to operate as designed, without making any claims about how an agent or person acts on its reports.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-18 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/dec7c232f8ba.smy@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": Feasibility: met }
~ Feasibility: met

The commit message confirms that the feasibility of the project has been met, indicating that smysl works as a self-contained library under an installable cargo subcommand.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-19 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/dec7c232f8ba.smy@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "S3, done: rationale packed into an agent's prompt did not change what the agent did" }
~ S3, done: rationale packed into an agent's prompt did not change what the agent did

The commit message states that packing rationale into an agent's prompt did not influence the agent's actions.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-20 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/dec7c232f8ba.smy@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "S4, done (2026-09-19): `check` ships advisory" }
~ S4, done (2026-09-19): `check` ships advisory

The commit message indicates that the `check` command has been implemented and is now shipping as an advisory tool.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-21 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/dec7c232f8ba.smy@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "S0, done (2026-09-20): the extraction figures exist, and they are figures about models" }
~ S0, done (2026-09-20): the extraction figures exist, and they are figures about models

The commit message confirms that the extraction figures have been established and are related to model performance.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-22 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/dec7c232f8ba.smy@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": Reassessed 2026-09-20 (D19): the project stops measuring models and measures the tool }
~ Reassessed 2026-09-20 (D19): the project stops measuring models and measures the tool

The commit message states that the project has reassessed its approach to measurement, focusing on the tool rather than the models.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-23 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/dec7c232f8ba.smy@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The model is the operator's choice, never the tool's" }
~ The model is the operator's choice, never the tool's

The commit message states that the model selection is left to the operator, with the tool not making any decisions about which model to use.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-24 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/dec7c232f8ba.smy@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Next: the tool-side acceptance in §6 and §7 (deterministic, model-free), then the operator's own benchmark (§8, item 11) so model choice is an informed decision by whoever installs this" }
~ Next: the tool-side acceptance in §6 and §7 (deterministic, model-free), then the operator's own benchmark …

The commit message outlines the next steps for the project, focusing on tool-side acceptance and providing an operator's benchmark for model selection.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-25 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/extractions/v1/856a434cf607.json@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": The README now leads with the seven deterministic commands rather than with extraction. }
