It focuses on the part that needs no model and is worth someone's time today.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-26 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/extractions/v1/856a434cf607.json@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": It also no longer implies `stale` works on a fresh clone. }
~ It also no longer implies `stale` works on a fresh clone.

Clarifies that `stale` reads a corpus, which is written by extraction.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-27 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/extractions/v1/856a434cf607.json@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": So `check` **ships advisory**: it prints findings and exits 0 unless `--strict`. }
~ `check` ships advisory: it prints findings and exits 0 unless `--strict`.

Acknowledges the limitations of the model's precision and advises caution.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-28 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/extractions/v1/856a434cf607.json@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": The model-dependent third is honest about being weak. }
~ `extract` is honest about being weak.

Discloses the limitations of the extraction process based on measured performance.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-29 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/extractions/v1/856a434cf607.json@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "What did work: **two-pass agreement** (170 and 192 flags became 96, and it removed every false flag on a real commit in development), which is why `check` runs two passes by default." }
~ Two-pass agreement is used by default for `check` to remove false flags.

Improves the precision of findings by ensuring two independent runs agree.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-30 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/extractions/v1/856a434cf607.json@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Staleness by item body hash. Reasoning is attached to code identity rather than to line ranges, so a function that moved is not stale and one that changed is." }
~ Staleness is detected by item body hash rather than line ranges.

Prevents false positives for functions that have merely moved.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-31 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/extractions/v1/856a434cf607.json@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "It ships its own instrument. `bench` measures the model *you* chose on *your* commits, and every published figure names the model it came from." }
~ `bench` measures the model you chose on your own commits.

Allows users to measure and verify the performance of their chosen models.

@decision d/g0d79d4a840b4-32 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/ceaa000d8f9e.smy@0d79d4a840b4 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": A cloned corpus is someone else's claim. Units carry the status the tool gave them; read `speculative` as what it says. }
